what is up everybody it's animak here  for anime opera and today i will be  breaking down the latest twist  in the seven deadly sins sequel a twist  that completely shocked  all of us long time seven deadly sins  fans  arthur and merlin were recently revealed  to be the villains of the seven deadly  sins sequel  and in the latest chapter we finally got  some information about how they might  have turned  into villains in fact arthur just  implied that he plans to eliminate  the remaining members of the seven  deadly sins  along with the four nights of the  apocalypse which is absolutely  crazy so let's get into it if you  enjoyed the seven deadly sins and four  nights of the apocalypse content  on this channel and you want to see more  you know what to do just leave a quick  like and comment  it only takes a second but it helps with  the youtube algorithm  and if you're new to anime uproar or  maybe watch our videos but you haven't  taken the time to subscribe yet  do me a favor and make this the video  that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on all  notifications remember you have to go  through the trouble of subscribing  hitting the bell and then selecting the  option that says all  if you don't do all of those things  you're still gonna miss a ton of our  videos even if you are subscribed it's  just how youtube works  you can also hit me up on twitter and  instagram  at animeopror finally this video will of  course contain seven deadly sins sequel  spoilers  so please proceed with caution you have  been warned  the latest chapter picks up inside the  throne room in camelot  where arthur is still berating ironside  for failing to complete his mission  arthur is determined to destroy leonis  for some reason  and he is disappointed that ironside  couldn't even defeat a child  even if that child happens to be one of  the four knights of the apocalypse  arthur then proceeds to use a terrifying  display of chaos power  to pierce into ironside's flesh and  practically tear him a limb from limb  this is a scene straight out of the most  terrifying horror movies  and man i have to say that chaos power  is the stuff of nightmares  i can't even show most of this stuff on  youtube it is that gruesome  as he mercilessly tortures ironside  arthur is ironically talking about how  camelot is a land with no pain and  no sadness a land where no one is  exposed to any kind of threat  or calamity uh what how are you saying  this while brutally torturing one of  your own men  this is just insane but if you thought  that was crazy  arthur then goes on to say something  even crazier he says that as long as the  remnants of the seven deadly sins  and the four knights of the apocalypse  are still around camelot  will never have true peace this implies  that arthur is going to try to take down  the remaining members of the seven  deadly sins  along with the four knights of the  apocalypse merlin appears to be on  arthur's side and escanor is  unfortunately no longer with us but that  still leaves  bonn gother king the end and of course  meliodas  as arthur's targets as crazy as arthur's  animosity towards the seven deadly sins  sounds to all of us who were fans of the  original series this is also an exciting  development for me personally because it  means that we might be seeing the  remaining five sins  in this sequel sooner than we thought if  arthur is the current main villain of  the story and he is targeting the seven  deadly sins along with the four knights  of the apocalypse  then it's safe to assume that we'll be  hearing from the seven deadly sins gang  sooner rather than later arthur says  that we must protect mankind from the  constant holy wars that have been taking  place  among the various races implying that he  is not necessarily interested in peace  between the different races  he seems interested in protecting and  freeing the humans in particular  and he isn't concerned about the  well-being of the other races  he is also determined to protect camelot  but camelot now appears to be located in  a completely different realm  from the rest of britannia it is as if  the giant palace of camelot  exists inside some sort of pocket  dimension created by chaos power  at the end of the original series arthur  set out to turn camelot  into an everlasting kingdom so perhaps  placing camelot  inside some sort of chaos realm is part  of arthur's plan  to make his kingdom eternal at any rate  arthur eventually decides to stop  torturing ironside and once ironside is  released his wounds are suddenly  completely healed and even the blood  that had spilled all over him is now  gone  arthur looks at ironside and laughs  telling ironside that hey  at least the torture took out all the  poison from your blood  and in that moment arthur looks like the  kind and friendly person that he  had been in the original series which to  be honest is even scarier than if he was  just completely evil  all of the time what is going on with  this man did chaos power drive him crazy  can't merlin help him in some way  ironside vows to successfully defeat  percival next time around  but arthur tells ironside that he has a  different mission  for him instead of fighting the four  knights of the apocalypse ironside's job  will be to search for arthur's  bride um okay ironside is clearly  surprised by this request from arthur  and i think  all of us readers are as well after all  of these crazy reveals  including the fact that arthur is a  villain that he is targeting the  remaining seven deadly sins and that he  seems to be trying to protect humans at  the expense of the  other races i don't think that any of us  were expecting arthur to just casually  ask  ironside to find him a wife also merlin  is  right there bro she's right there  meanwhile as i said merlin is present  throughout this entire scene but she  doesn't seem to actually say  anything she is too quiet suspiciously  quiet  i get the strong feeling that she  doesn't support what's happening with  arthur and she doesn't agree  with his actions but for some reason she  has to go along with them we have no  idea what  that reason is and that makes this whole  situation  all the more mysterious the focus of the  chapter then switches back to sistana  and the aftermath of the battle against  ironside  anne's father thanks percival and the  gang for protecting sustana  even though there is a lot of physical  damage to the town thankfully none of  the citizens  died as a result of the battle and that  is the most important thing  sin is once again asked about his ally  or allies and where they went  but he is dodgy and he refuses to answer  this is getting pretty frustrating to me  personally because i was expecting a big  bond reveal but i guess we'll have to  wait a bit longer  anne's father then explains that he is  well acquainted with ironside  and percival's grandpa because they  served camelot as holy knights  alongside anne's mother in the image  that we see of anne's mother with  ironside and percival's grandpa  in the background we can also see arthur  merlin and  nanashi that samurai guy who appeared in  the original seven deadly sins series  during the visel festival  arc it seems that nanashi decided to  serve king arthur in camelot  after the original series ended nanashi  is a pretty random character to just  like throw in there but  personally i do appreciate every  reference to the original series so it's  all good with me now the weird thing  is anne's mother had once described  ironside  as a noble and upright man who was  always striving to do  good so clearly something has changed  drastically with ironside  in the past 16 years and that very much  echoes  arthur's own transformation from  kind-hearted hero  and ally of the sins to a villain king  who apparently wants to destroy the  seven deadly sins  roughly 16 years ago some major event  must have occurred in camelot  something that completely changed not  only king arthur but also many of his  men  including ironside did the power of  chaos suddenly take control of arthur  and corrupt his mind  did some impostor manage to somehow take  control of arthur did something else  happen to genuinely change arthur's mind  about the seven deadly sins and the holy  wars i'm betting that the power of chaos  will prove to be the key to  understanding what really happened  but we'll have to wait and see how  things play out the chapter ends as anne  decides to leave systana  and join percival sin and nacienza and  dani on their journey  and dreams of becoming a great holy  night one day just like her mother  but the fight with ironside has taught  her that she still has a long way to go  so ann is going to set off from sistana  and begin  more intense training and since percival  and the squad  are already there it makes sense for  them all to travel together  so after a tearful goodbye with her  father and joins the squad  and the adventure continues personally i  really like anne i think she's cool and  very badass  and i think she will make a good  addition to the squad her name  anne galahad is likely a reference to  sir galahad  one of the knights of the round table in  arthurian legend  so it makes sense that anne would play  an important part in the story  that said as much as i do like the  current squad  i definitely want to see tristan and  lancelot making their appearance  sometime soon not to mention the ogs  like bonn and meliodas  let me know what you guys think why  would arthur turn against  the seven deadly sins and does the fact  that he directly mentioned them as his  targets  mean that some of them are about to  return to the story sooner  rather than later also what's the deal  with ironside  how did he go from a noble knight who  does only good things to an evil villain  who murdered his own father  tried to murder his son and nearly  sacrificed an  entire town finally when is the main  squad going to meet up with the other  knights of the apocalypse definitely  share your thoughts  down in the comments below if you  enjoyed this video and you want to see  more summer daily sins and four nights  of the apocalypse videos here on the  channel  please leave that like and comment it  only takes a second but it helps a lot  then if you're new to anime pro or maybe  you watch our videos but you just  haven't taken the time to subscribe yet  do me a favor make this the video that  you subscribe and hit  that notification bell to turn on all  notifications  you can also hit me up on twitter and  instagram at  animeopror i want to give a big thank  you to all of our  anime uproar patrons for making videos  like this one possible  special thank you to alpha sigma he is  an absolute mad lad  and disciple of lord twigo himself  and i can't forget all of our the one  tier patrons the ones who rise above  all other clans including ingrata pate  heffa  al-jatal hirokami and water the toasted  chi the spike  emperor otaku spidey life chanel  tungsten tarkis baked buddhist cody  hebert and monkey d  quilly finally thank you also to our pro  hero tier patrons including the one and  only gilgamesh the red haired raven  angel crews  rathune de ora very gucci alicia octor  bonnie parks joanne garcia techno ted  fat boy games corey mcgowan and soul ray  slice and dice  if you enjoy our videos and you feel  that they provide value to you consider  supporting us  on patreon even a single dollar will  give you access to our patron exclusive  discord and your name will appear in our  videos  along with these legendary people as  always thank you guys so much for  watching and until next time  see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you
 

